# The trivia bank is the product, not a public asset. Nothing in the browser loads it
# (the homepage counter reads /data/trivia-count.json instead), so serve a 404 rather
# than handing the whole question bank to anyone who guesses the URL.
/data/trivia-library.json    /404  404
/data/trivia-review-*.json   /404  404

# Everything below is source, not site. It all sits in the deploy root, so it was being
# served to anyone who guessed a filename: the full database schema and every RLS policy,
# both Workers, and the seed scripts. Combined with the public anon key printed in every
# page, a schema dump is a real head start for anyone poking at the database.
#
# seed-trivia-TEST.sql matters most: its first two lines DELETE the entire shared trivia
# library before inserting test rows. It has no business being on the public internet.
/supabase/*                  /404  404
/worker/*                    /404  404
/tools/*                     /404  404
/*.sql                       /404  404
/*.py                        /404  404
/data/musical-library-full.json  /404  404
/data/generated/*            /404  404
